(; doc: An `AddSubgroup` is closed under inverse. ;)
(; //LEAN:AddSubgroup.neg_mem ;)
AddSubgroup__neg_mem : (G : Set) -> (_ : Proof (AddGroup G)) -> (H : Elem (AddSubgroup G)) -> (x1 : Elem G) -> (h : Proof (Membership__mem G (AddSubgroup G) H x1)) -> Proof (Membership__mem G (AddSubgroup G) H (Neg__neg G x1)).

(; doc: Pull an additive subgroup back to an opposite additive subgroup along `AddOpposite.unop` ;)
(; //LEAN:AddSubgroup.op ;)
AddSubgroup__op : (G : Set) -> (H : Elem (AddSubgroup G)) -> Elem (AddSubgroup (AddOpposite G)).

(; doc: A version of `Set.pi` for `AddSubgroup`s. Given an index set `I` and a family of submodules `s : Π i, AddSubgroup f i`, `pi I s` is the `AddSubgroup` of dependent functions `f : Π i, f i` such that `f i` belongs to `pi I s` whenever `i ∈ I`. ;)
(; //LEAN:AddSubgroup.pi ;)
AddSubgroup__pi : (X : Set) -> (f : (Elem X -> Set)) -> (I : Elem (powerset X)) -> (H : ((i1 : Elem X) -> AddSubgroup (f i1))) -> Elem (AddSubgroup ((i : Elem X) -> f i)).

(; doc: Given `AddSubgroup`s `H`, `K` of `AddGroup`s `A`, `B` respectively, `H × K` as an `AddSubgroup` of `A × B`. ;)
(; //LEAN:AddSubgroup.prod ;)
AddSubgroup__prod : (G : Set) -> (N : Set) -> (H : Elem (AddSubgroup G)) -> (K : Elem (AddSubgroup N)) -> Elem (AddSubgroup (Prod G N)).

(; //LEAN:AddSubgroup.quotientAddSubgroupOfEmbeddingOfLE._proof_2 ;)
